 on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Florida's governorship is open for the first time since 2018, with term limits ending Ron DeSantis's tenure. Republican Byron Donalds faces Democrat David Jolly, a former Republican congressman, along with several independents and a Libertarian. Mid-October polling averages put Donalds ahead by roughly four to five points, though individual surveys vary, with one university poll showing a double-digit lead and a Republican internal poll showing six.\n\nDonalds has raised about $13.8 million and benefits from running in a state with a five-point Republican lean, while the national midterm environment tilts Democratic. Jolly is counting on crossover appeal and undecided Black and independent voters, and faces questions about past ties to an alleged fraudster. Most expert raters call the race Lean Republican, with one calling it a tossup, and prediction markets give Jolly roughly a one-in-five chance. No televised debates were held, limiting late opportunities for either side.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1709, "margin": -5.38}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2654, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2923, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2636, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1983, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2414, "margin": -3.8}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2597, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2217, "margin": -4.8}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2584, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.252, "margin": -4.3}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2745, "margin": -3.8}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.2552, "margin": -4.2}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.2498, "margin": -4.2}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.2281, "margin": -4.2}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.2329, "margin": -4.2}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.2195, "margin": -4.2}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.2688, "margin": -3